## 3. AI Evaluation

### 3.1 Current AI Implementation

| AI Feature | Screen | Implementation Quality | Notes |
|-----------|--------|----------------------|-------|
| **Smart Search** suggesting templates | Template Selection | ⚠️ Mock | Triggered by keyword matching ("defect"/"deviation"), not a real AI model. Shows a blue suggestion banner. |
| **AI Classification** recommendation | Document Creation | ⚠️ Mock | Shows "AI: Recommended based on intent" label but always returns the same suggestion regardless of input. |
| **Duplicate Detection** on upload | Template Selection | ⚠️ Mock | Simulates a scanning delay then always returns "Quality Deviation Report – Line 2 (v10)". Not connected to any real comparison engine. |
| **Review Insights** (summary, critical points) | Review Flow | ⚠️ Mock | Hardcoded AI insights: summary, critical change detection, compliance checklist. Not dynamically generated. |
| **Pre-filled Content** from upload | Document Creation | ⚠️ Mock | When routed via upload, shows pre-filled text. Static content, not extracted from actual file. |

### 3.2 AI Maturity Assessment

```
Current Level:  ████░░░░░░  Level 2 of 5 — "Visual Mock"
                
Level 1: No AI              ░░░░░░░░░░
Level 2: Visual Mock Only   ████░░░░░░  ← YOU ARE HERE
Level 3: Basic Functionality ░░░░░░░░░░
Level 4: Intelligent System  ░░░░░░░░░░
Level 5: Autonomous/Agentic  ░░░░░░░░░░
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> All AI features are **UI-only mockups** — they display convincing AI-style interfaces but are not connected to any ML model, LLM API, or intelligent processing backend. For a market-ready product, these need to be connected to real AI services.

### 3.3 Missing AI Capabilities for Market Readiness

| # | AI Capability | Impact | Description |
|---|-------------|--------|-------------|
| 1 | **Conversational Document Search** "Ask Your Documents" | 🔴 Critical | Users type natural language questions and get synthesized answers from across the document repository. (e.g., "What is the max temperature limit for Line 2?") |
| 2 | **Real AI Document Classification** | 🔴 Critical | Auto-classify uploaded docs by type, category, and metadata using an ML model trained on your document corpus. |
| 3 | **Intelligent Content Extraction (IDP)** | High | OCR + AI to extract structured data from uploaded documents (tables, forms, signatures, dates). |
| 4 | **AI-Generated Summaries** | High | Auto-generate executive summaries for long SOPs, manuals, and reports — connected to a real LLM. |
| 5 | **Smart Change Detection** | High | AI-powered diff that highlights semantic changes (not just text), explains impact, and flags compliance risks. |
| 6 | **Predictive Workflow Routing** | High | AI learns from past approvals to suggest optimal reviewers and predict approval timeline. |
| 7 | **Anomaly & Risk Detection** | High | Flag unusual patterns: unauthorized access attempts, bulk downloads, modification patterns outside norms. |
| 8 | **Auto-Tagging & Metadata Enrichment** | High | Automatically extract and assign metadata tags (equipment names, chemical names, lot numbers) from document content. |
| 9 | **Compliance Gap Analysis** | High | AI scans documents against regulatory frameworks and highlights missing sections or non-compliant language. |
| 10 | **AI Training Content Generation** | Medium | Generate quiz questions and training materials from SOP content for the training management module. |
| 11 | **Document Expiry Prediction** | Medium | Predict which documents are likely to need revision based on change patterns and regulatory updates. |
| 12 | **AI Copilot for Document Authoring** | Medium | In-editor AI assistant that helps write, format, and ensure compliance of document content. |

